description:
Same treatment as pochoir B.1, for the weighting pair. NO VALUE CHANGES.

Files: test/example_gen_pixel_with_grid_task13_coarse.json and test/example_gen_pixel_with_grid_task13_fine.json

Add a "_description" string to each stating:
  - this is the WEIGHTING (unit probe) config, and which spacing it transcribes;
  - it deliberately carries NO GridPotential and NO CathodePotential: the weighting potential is a dimensionless unit probe in [0,1], not volts, so the cathode formula in the drift configs does not apply here;
  - the probe is Npixels=17 at a 4.4mm pitch = 74.8mm transverse, non-periodic (edges fix,fix,fix) so phi_w decays to ~0 at the tile edges rather than wrapping;
  - the same coarse/fine pad-gap split rationale as B.1 if the two files differ on pixelSize/pixelGap -- CHECK the actual values first and only state it if true.

Verify with json.load that both files still parse and that every pre-existing key is byte-identical.

